- Functions should be small (max 20 lines)
- Functions should do one thing only
- Functions should have no more than 3 parameters
- Use descriptive function names that explain what they do
- Avoid flag arguments (boolean parameters that change behavior)
- Prefer command-query separation: functions either do something or return something, not both
- Extract try-catch blocks into separate functions
- Don't repeat yourself (DRY principle)